{
 "method": "Simulated golfer: plans like the AI and swings with a fixed human-like error model (skill 0.35 poor, 0.6 average, 0.9 skilled). 9-hole rounds across all seven courses (front and back nines alternate); paired random draws per round index (strike dice on their own stream); 3000 rounds per cell; per-18 values are twice the 9-hole means. Tier differences are paired against Common with the same swing, planning and conditions. Conditions: calm fairway play (no wind, every lie through the green played as a flat fairway lie), normal (each course's own wind and the real lies), and wind and rough (a 10 to 20 mph gusty wind and every fairway lie played as rough). Archetypes, settings and pros play normal conditions. Tier benefits (data/tierBenefits.js) apply to the shots and the plan: a crosswind moves a higher tier's ball less and rough, sand and bad lies cost it less; the golfer does not use the spin pad, so the third benefit, the wider spin and shape range, is not in these numbers. Every tier carries the table carry in this build and the guide shows it, so the golfer plans the same way with every tier.",
